identifier: ParaSoft
name: ParaSoft Airbraking Technologies
abstract: >-
  Softbody parachutes. Canopies leave their pack, stream out, fill with air, breathe,
  swing in the wind, collapse onto the ground and ride the waves - on the parachutes you
  already have, with drag left exactly as your parachute mod computes it.
description: >-
  ParaSoft Airbraking Technologies turns every round parachute canopy into a softbody.
  Each canopy is simulated as cloth on its seams, with suspension lines, a pilot chute and
  ram air filling it, and the part's own canopy mesh follows the simulation - so its
  textures, RealChute's canopy choices and Custom Parachute Message's encoded canopies all
  carry over.


  Canopies deploy like real ones: the pack leaves the part, lines pay out, the canopy
  streams and then fills crown first; reefed chutes stay reefed until the module disreefs
  them. They react to their surroundings - thick air, thin air, supersonic flight and
  vacuum all look different with nothing special-cased; wind from Kerbal Weather Project
  (or any wind registered with FAR) moves them; they collapse onto terrain, buildings and
  craft, float on the sea and ride Scatterer's waves.


  Drag is never changed. Stock ModuleParachute, RealChute and FAR's RealChuteLite keep
  computing and applying all of their own forces; ParaSoft only simulates and draws the
  canopy and never pushes back on the craft.
$kref: '#/ckan/github/CritZitGaming/KSP-ParaSoft'
$vref: '#/ckan/ksp-avc/ParaSoft/ParaSoft.version'
